+# Bulk import of customer contacts
+
+Not run or tested: there was no PHP/database available, so this is untested code.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `Z_ImportCustContacts.php` (new): the import page.
+  - CSV columns: `debtorno, contactname, role, phoneno, email, notes, statement`.
+  - The template is a real CSV download (`?gettemplate=1`) with those columns.
+  - Matching is on customer + contact name. Name comparison uses the database collation, so it is case-insensitive.
+  - Rows are processed one by one. A bad row is skipped and reported with its line number and reason; it does not abort the file. A database error rolls back the whole import.
+  - The summary shows added, updated, already up to date, and skipped. Each skipped row has a reason: unknown customer, missing name, value too long (the column is named), invalid e-mail, not allowed to update. Other reasons are wrong column count and bad statement flag.
+- Permission to update: new security token **21** "Update existing customer contacts when importing". The administrator grants or withdraws it in Setup → Security Roles like any other token.
+  - The page itself needs the usual token 15, like the other imports, and sits under Utilities → Maintenance.
+  - Users with 15 but without 21 can only add. Rows that would change an existing contact are skipped as "not allowed to update".
+- `sql/updates/44.php` (new): for existing databases. It adds the token, the script (security 15) and the menu item.
+- `install/sql/data/{securitytokens,scripts,menuitems}.sql` and `install/sql/demo.sql`: the same three rows for new installs. The installer sets `DBUpdateNumber` to the highest update file, so update 44 does not run on a fresh install and these files must carry the rows themselves.
+
+## Ambiguities and how I resolved them
+
+- **Token 21 is granted to no role by default.** Nobody can update until the administrator grants it. This is the safe reading of "only people the administrator allows".
+- **Rows identical to the existing contact** are counted as "already up to date", not as updated or skipped, whoever runs the import. They change nothing, so they are not a sensitive update. This is a fourth count beyond the three requested.
+- **Duplicate rows in one file** for the same customer and name: the first adds the contact. The second is then an existing-contact row. It updates if the user has the token and is skipped otherwise.
+- **Several existing contacts with the same customer and name:** all of them are updated together.
+- **E-mail:** may be blank, but a blank address with statement = 1 is skipped as an invalid e-mail, because statements cannot be sent without it.
+- **Statement flag:** 1/0, yes/no, y/n, true/false, or empty (treated as 0). Anything else is skipped.
+- **Customer code** is matched with the database collation (case-insensitive) and stored as it appears in the customer record.
+- **Menu rows** are inserted for every security role, as the existing `NewMenuItem` helper does. Access is still enforced by page token 15.
